1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,907
Welcome to KFAR Marketplace.

2
00:00:01,907 --> 00:00:10,210
This is a complete overview of your multi-vendor e-commerce platform, built for the Village of Peace community in Dimona, Israel.

3
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:23,460
KFAR Marketplace connects six local vendors with your community, supporting both Hebrew and English, multiple payment methods including community currency called Braysheet, and a full loyalty rewards system.

4
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:25,381
Let me walk you through the platform.

5
00:00:25,381 --> 00:00:27,250
First, the technology.

6
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:32,552
KFAR runs on Next.js 15, which is a modern React framework.

7
00:00:32,552 --> 00:00:45,131
It's backed by a PostgreSQL database with 24 tables, secure JWT authentication with bcrypt password hashing, and Tailwind CSS for a beautiful responsive design.

8
00:00:45,131 --> 00:00:50,802
The platform has 133 API routes and 205 static pages.

9
00:00:50,802 --> 00:01:06,947
Your six active vendors are: Teva Deli with 32 products, Queen's Cuisine with 25 products, People's Store with 18 products, Garden of Light with 14 products, Gahn Delight with 12 products, and VOP Shop with 12 products.

10
00:01:06,947 --> 00:01:09,460
That's 113 products total.

11
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:18,565
Each vendor has their own dashboard where they can manage products, view orders, track analytics, create promotions, and generate QR codes.

12
00:01:18,565 --> 00:01:23,500
Vendors log in at their dedicated portal and get a full business management suite.

13
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,802
For payments, the platform supports four methods.

14
00:01:26,802 --> 00:01:30,315
Cash on delivery is the default and is fully active.

15
00:01:30,315 --> 00:01:36,236
Braysheet tokens, your community digital currency, are active with QR-based wallets.

16
00:01:36,236 --> 00:01:39,486
Bank transfer is active with provided details.

17
00:01:39,486 --> 00:01:48,565
And credit card processing via YPAY, an Israeli payment gateway, is ready in sandbox mode, just waiting for production credentials.

18
00:01:48,565 --> 00:02:03,723
The order flow works like this: A customer places an order, payment is processed, the vendor accepts the order, prepares it, marks it as ready for pickup, and then when the customer picks it up, it's marked as completed and loyalty points are earned.

19
00:02:03,723 --> 00:02:10,276
For email, KFAR has its own dedicated email server with DKIM signing for reliable deliverability.

20
00:02:10,276 --> 00:02:21,763
You have three email accounts: noreply at kfarapp dot com for system emails, admin at kfarapp dot com for admin communications, and support at kfarapp dot com for customer support.

21
00:02:21,763 --> 00:02:34,605
There are 10 email templates covering order confirmations, status updates, vendor alerts, welcome emails, loyalty notifications, password resets, promotions, and QR loyalty cards.

22
00:02:34,605 --> 00:02:37,881
All templates are available in both English and Hebrew.

23
00:02:37,881 --> 00:02:40,618
The admin dashboard gives you full control.

24
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:45,565
You can see revenue, orders, and customer overviews from the main dashboard.

25
00:02:45,565 --> 00:03:03,855
Manage your vendors, create product bundles, track all orders, run CRM for customer management and segmentation, manage user accounts, create and approve promotions, send broadcast notifications to all users, review driver applications, and configure store settings.

26
00:03:03,855 --> 00:03:08,013
Speaking of drivers, there's a complete driver application system.

27
00:03:08,013 --> 00:03:12,710
Community members can apply to become delivery drivers through a public form.

28
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:16,710
Applications go to the admin queue for approval or rejection.

29
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:23,013
The CRM system tracks customer profiles with orders, points, and activity timelines.

30
00:03:23,013 --> 00:03:29,460
You can create auto and manual customer segments for targeting, and view full interaction histories.

31
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:44,315
The loyalty system has three tiers: Bronze for zero to 499 points with base rewards, Silver for 500 to 1499 points with a 5 percent bonus, and Gold for 1500 plus points with a 10 percent bonus.

32
00:03:44,315 --> 00:03:52,828
Customers earn points on every purchase, get 50 welcome bonus points on registration, and can redeem points for discount coupons.

33
00:03:52,828 --> 00:03:58,368
For performance, KFAR uses Cloudflare as a global CDN and security layer.

34
00:03:58,368 --> 00:04:10,171
Cloudflare provides SSL encryption, DDoS protection, intelligent caching at edge locations worldwide, and gzip compression achieving 87 percent size reduction.

35
00:04:10,171 --> 00:04:21,618
Static assets are cached for up to 365 days, authentication endpoints have rate limiting, and security headers include HSTS and Content Security Policy.

36
00:04:21,618 --> 00:04:25,644
This means fast load times for your community no matter where they are.

37
00:04:26,569 --> 00:04:30,480
The platform supports full Hebrew and English translation.

38
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:41,230
There's a language toggle in the header, RTL layout auto-applied for Hebrew, and an AI Shopping Assistant powered by Google Gemini with voice support in both languages.

39
00:04:41,230 --> 00:04:43,638
Deploying updates is straightforward.

40
00:04:43,638 --> 00:04:48,046
Pull the latest code, build the application, and restart the service.

41
00:04:48,046 --> 00:04:54,743
The platform follows modern DevOps best practices with version control and zero-downtime deployments.

42
00:04:54,743 --> 00:04:56,414
That's KFAR Marketplace.

43
00:04:56,414 --> 00:05:00,519
A complete, production-ready multi-vendor e-commerce platform.

44
00:05:00,519 --> 00:05:05,861
Community powered, beautifully designed, and ready to serve the Village of Peace.

45
00:05:05,861 --> 00:05:07,572
Thank you for choosing KFAR.
